EXPERIMENT 3
WEBSITE MIRRORING USING HTTRACK
==================================================

AIM

To demonstrate how HTTrack can be used to download and mirror a website locally for offline access and analysis.

DESCRIPTION

HTTrack is an open-source offline browser utility that enables users to download entire websites to a local directory. It replicates the original site's structure, including HTML, images, CSS, and other media files. This experiment shows how HTTrack can be used to create a local copy of a website and access it without an internet connection.

PROCEDURE

1. Install HTTrack

   1. Download HTTrack from the official website.
   2. Install the software and launch WinHTTrack (for Windows users).

2. Create a new project

   1. Click Next to start a new project.
   2. Enter a project name (e.g., myWebsiteCopy) and select a base path to save files.

3. Enter website URL

   1. Input the URL of the website to be mirrored (e.g., https://example.com).
   2. Multiple URLs can be added if needed.

4. Configure options

   1. Select Download website(s) as the action.
   2. Optionally set filters to include or exclude certain file types.

5. Start mirroring

   1. Click Finish to begin the download process.
   2. HTTrack will crawl the website and save its content locally.

6. View the mirrored site

   1. Open the saved directory.
   2. Double-click index.html to browse the site offline using a web browser.

OUTPUT

A fully functional offline copy of the selected website is created in the specified directory. The site can be accessed without an internet connection, and its structure and content remain intact for review or analysis.


